TAP version 14
# Subtest: confidence-adjusted ranking rewards supported quality rather than a single five-star vote
    ok 1 - Bayesian support and confidence penalty defeat the one-vote winner
    ok 2 - the shared PostgreSQL/Lagrange SQL projection uses the richer score
    1..2
ok 1 - confidence-adjusted ranking rewards supported quality rather than a single five-star vote # time=2.037ms

# Subtest: replica reduction implements the exact shared ranking formula
    ok 1 - service replicas and grouped-SQL paths produce the same order
    ok 2 - rank 1 score is identical
    ok 3 - rank 2 score is identical
    ok 4 - rank 3 score is identical
    1..4
ok 2 - replica reduction implements the exact shared ranking formula # time=1.24ms

# Subtest: service and grouped-SQL ranking share the movie-id tie-break
    ok 1 - fixture reaches the exact-score tie
    ok 2 - should be equivalent
    ok 3 - shared movie-id order cannot diverge at the top-N boundary
    1..3
ok 3 - service and grouped-SQL ranking share the movie-id tie-break # time=4.756ms

# Subtest: confidence-adjusted runtime config is explicit and validated
    ok 1 - implicit ranking priors are rejected
    ok 2 - the documented ranking policy is accepted
    1..2
ok 4 - confidence-adjusted runtime config is explicit and validated # time=3.978ms

# Subtest: three-way report compares correctness and transfer shape without a misleading speedup
